      <h2>Most directories sell placement. We measure firms, and publish exactly how.</h2>
      <p>Every sub-score on every profile shows the evidence it came from and the date it was
        read. A firm that disagrees can appeal, free, answered within 30 days. Correcting
        anything we published that is wrong is free and always will be.</p>
      <div class="hm-cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn--white" href="/methodology/">Read the methodology</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost-night" href="/guides/">See the research</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="hm-rules">
      <li><b>Gates before points.</b> A firm with an open disciplinary action cannot be certified at any score.</li>
      <li><b>Evidence before claims.</b> If we could not read it, we do not publish it. Sites we could not read are named, not counted as empty.</li>
      <li><b>Local before national.</b> Search authority is a percentile of the firm's own city, so a Lakeland firm is not measured against Manhattan.</li>
      <li><b>Nothing here is for sale.</b> No points, no gate, no tier, no position in any ranked list.</li>
