<section class="section section--paper">
  <div class="container faq-split">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions people ask first</span>
      <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Before you hire anyone</h2>
      <p style="margin-top:14px;max-width:38ch">Short answers to the questions we hear most. Every
        guide is reviewed by a licensed attorney in the relevant state.</p>
      <a class="link" href="/guides/" style="margin-top:20px">Browse all {guideCount} studies</a>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details open><summary>How much does a lawyer cost?</summary><div>It depends on the matter. Injury firms almost always work on contingency, typically a third, nothing up front. Divorce, criminal defense and business work are usually hourly or flat fee. Every profile shows the fee model before you call.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Do law firms pay to be listed here?</summary><div>No. Firms appear because we found them and read their public record, and being listed costs nothing. The Certification Score, the eligibility gates and the tier cannot be bought or edited by anyone. A firm that wants to manage its own profile can take an optional annual listing, and sponsored placements are always labeled and never appear inside a ranked list.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Is a certified firm better than a highly rated one?</summary><div>Ratings tell you how clients felt. Certification tells you the attorneys are licensed and undisciplined, and that what the firm publishes about itself holds up. The best firms have both, and the rankings weight them together.</div></details>
      <details><summary>What happens when I request a consultation?</summary><div>Your message goes straight to the firm. We do not sell it to other lawyers and we take no referral fee.{freeConsultShare !== null && <> {freeConsultShare}% of the firms published here offer the first consultation free.</>} How quickly a firm replies is up to the firm; we do not measure it yet, so we do not promise it.</div></details>
      <details><summary>What if a firm loses its certification?</summary><div>If a public disciplinary action appears or verified reviews fall below our threshold, the badge is removed within 30 days and the firm drops out of ranked lists until it re-qualifies.</div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script define:vars={{ searchIndex }}>
  // The hero search routes in the browser against the pages that exist, and says so when it
  // cannot. Unchanged in behaviour from the page this replaced.
  const form = document.getElementById('firm-search');
  const note = document.getElementById('search-note');
  if (form) {
    form.addEventListener('submit', e => {
      const q = (document.getElementById('q')?.value ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();
      const loc = (document.getElementById('loc')?.value ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();
      const city = searchIndex.cities.find(c =>
        loc && (c.name.toLowerCase().includes(loc) || loc.includes(c.city.toLowerCase())));
      const practice = searchIndex.practices.find(p =>
        q && (p.name.toLowerCase().includes(q) || q.includes(p.name.toLowerCase())));
      if (city && practice) { e.preventDefault(); location.href = `/cities/${city.slug}/${practice.slug}/`; return; }
      if (city) { e.preventDefault(); location.href = city.href; return; }
      if (practice) { e.preventDefault(); location.href = practice.href; return; }
      if ((q || loc) && note) {
        e.preventDefault();
        note.hidden = false;
        note.textContent = 'We do not publish that combination yet. Browse the cities we do.';
      }
    });
  }
</script>

